<article class="env-example" id="00TY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00TY">Example <span data-tag="00TY">10.140.8</span>.</a> Lemma <a href="/tag/00TX" data-tag="00TX">10.140.7</a> does not hold in characteristic $p > 0$. The standard examples are the ring maps </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{F}_ p \longrightarrow \mathbf{F}_ p[x]/(x^ p)  \]
</div>
  <p> whose module of differentials is free but is clearly not smooth, and the ring map ($p > 2$) </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{F}_ p(t) \to \mathbf{F}_ p(t)[x, y]/(x^ p + y^2 + \alpha )  \]
</div>
  <p> which is not smooth at the prime $\mathfrak q = (y, x^ p + \alpha )$ but is regular. </p>
</article>